message.content:
I found two likely periapical lesions. Neither is certain. I enhanced and enlarged crops of the image to look for them.

```json
{"lesions": [
  {"box": [0.297, 0.725, 0.328, 0.770], "pai": 3},
  {"box": [0.457, 0.367, 0.483, 0.413], "pai": 3}
]}
```

1. **Lower right molar with root canal fillings, next to the bridge (PAI 3):** below the root tips, the bone has an ill-defined dark area where some mineral seems to be lost. There is no clear well-defined radiolucent area, so I scored it 3 rather than 4.
2. **Upper right central incisor with a post and crown (PAI 3):** there is a darker area around the root tip. It overlaps the dark air shadow that runs across this part of the image, so this one is less certain.

I left out the lower left molar with the filling. It has a dark spot in the crown that looks like decay, but I couldn't see a clear periapical change below its roots. These grades come from one panoramic image and should be checked against a periapical radiograph and a clinical exam.
